.{
    .name = .notary,
    .fingerprint = 0x1c66b255a707070,
    .version = "0.1.0",
    .minimum_zig_version = "0.16.0",
    .dependencies = .{
        // The Native SDK framework, pinned to a commit. `native eject` wrote a
        // machine-local `.path` into somebody's npm install here, which is
        // reproducible on exactly one computer: every CI runner and every
        // contributor built against whatever CLI version happened to be
        // installed, and a release was whatever npm served that afternoon.
        //
        // Bump this and the CLI version in .github/workflows/*.yml IN THE SAME
        // COMMIT. The automation harness refuses to read a snapshot when the
        // CLI and the framework speak different protocol versions, and moving
        // one alone does not fail the build: it silently breaks every live
        // test.
        //
        // A fork rather than vercel-labs/native, for patches that are all in
        // the renderer and the input path Linux presents with. Two of them are
        // Notary's:
        //
        //   * a codepoint the bundled faces do not carry is painted as a solid
        //     block, and the approval prompt shows the CLIENT's name, so a
        //     client named in Japanese would be a row of rectangles on the
        //     screen where somebody decides whether to sign
        //     (vercel-labs/native#421);
        //   * an app could not fill the sans medium and bold faces, so every
        //     heading in this window was flat on Linux
        //     (vercel-labs/native#423).
        //
        // The rest it gets without asking: colour emoji, scroll input
        // coalesced to one event a frame (#440), and a faster software
        // rasteriser (#442, #443). A detented wheel notch that travels instead
        // of jumping (#441) is in the tree too, and stays off here because the
        // window sets no `wheel_ease_ms`.
        //
        // It is v0.11.0 plus upstream #688 plus those patches. PATCHES.md in
        // the fork is the tracker: a row per patch with its upstream issue and
        // how to drop it when that issue closes. The commit is on the branch
        // `sdk-0.11.0`, so this does not depend on one tag surviving.
        .native_sdk = .{
            .url = "git+https://github.com/zig-nostr/native.git#caa09b31b0fcc6ab6e75660e370cf18373a6afd4",
            .hash = "native_sdk-0.1.0-hzDzQtY-SQNMo1tz2hay2oYMrxw2JwPltLKZDdildHyj",
        },
    },
    .paths = .{ "build.zig", "build.zig.zon", "src", "assets", "app.zon", "app.linux.zon" },
}
